 "narration": [
  {
   "text": "Long ago, there lived a mighty king named Kauśika.",
   "start": 6.625,
   "end": 11.593
  },
  {
   "text": "One day, hunting with his army, he came to the forest hermitage of the sage Vasiṣṭha.",
   "start": 12.343,
   "end": 19.711
  },
  {
   "text": "The sage welcomed them all, and through his sacred cow Nandinī, he fed the entire army.",
   "start": 20.461,
   "end": 29.221
  },
  {
   "text": "The king wanted the wondrous cow for himself. When Vasiṣṭha refused, he tried to take her by force.",
   "start": 29.971,
   "end": 38.539
  },
  {
   "text": "But every arrow, every weapon, fell silent before the sage's staff.",
   "start": 39.289,
   "end": 45.361
  },
  {
   "text": "Kauśika understood. The power of a sage was greater than the power of any king.",
   "start": 46.361,
   "end": 53.681
  },
  {
   "text": "So he laid down his crown, and went into the forest to become a sage himself.",
   "start": 54.431,
   "end": 61.247
  },
  {
   "text": "For years he meditated. Pride, desire and anger tested him. Again and again, he fell.",
   "start": 62.247,
   "end": 72.135
  },
  {
   "text": "And each time, he began again.",
   "start": 72.885,
   "end": 76.197
  },
  {
   "text": "At last his mind became as still and clear as the dawn. Even Vasiṣṭha bowed to him, and called him Brahmarṣi, a great seer.",
   "start": 77.197,
   "end": 89.413
  },
  {
   "text": "In that stillness, Viśvāmitra saw a prayer of light. Not for power, but for an awakened mind.",
   "start": 90.163,
   "end": 98.563
  },
  {
   "text": "The Gāyatrī.",
   "start": 99.313,
   "end": 101.185
  }
 ]
}